course: dictionary
lesson: 5196
title: Jaguar in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A jaguar is a noun, a name for a thing, here a big wild cat. The words around it show which meaning is meant. «The jaguar has the strongest bite for its size of any big cat» tells you it is an animal, because only an animal has a bite and hunts for food.
explain: Capital letters are a clue too. Jaguar with a capital J can be the name of a car make, as in «Jaguar is a British make of car». In a story, «Jaguar roars for his Mother» uses a capital J because it is a character's name, but the words around it show that he is a cat.
explain: Read the nearby words. «The Pantanal in Brazil is the world's biggest tropical wetland, where jaguars hunt caimans and capybaras» tells you the jaguar lives in a wet place and hunts other animals. Ask yourself: what would fit here? A wild cat fits. A car does not hunt.
fact: A jaguar is a big, powerful wild cat of Central and South America.
fact: Jaguars have golden fur covered in rosettes, which are spots with dots inside them.
fact: Jaguars are strong swimmers and hunt in rainforests and swamps, catching capybaras, fish, turtles and caimans.
fact: The jaguar is the largest cat in the Americas and has the strongest bite for its size of any big cat.
fact: Jaguar with a capital J can also be a British make of expensive car.
exercise: «The jaguar has the strongest bite for its size of any big cat.» What kind of thing is a jaguar here? | A capybara | A swamp | A car | *A wild cat
exercise: Where do jaguars hunt? | Mountain tops of snow | Town car parks | *Rainforests and swamps | Deserts and ice fields
exercise: Jaguar with a capital J is also the name of a famous car. Which meaning fits the car? | A kind of fish | *A British make of expensive car | A giant rodent | A big wild cat with golden fur
test: «Jaguars are strong swimmers and hunt in swamps.» What does swamp most likely mean? | A cold lake covered in ice | A dry desert | A tall tree | *A wet, muddy place
test: «Its golden fur is covered in rosettes.» What is a rosette on a jaguar? | A fish scale | *A spot with dots inside it | A long tail | A bright red stripe
exam: Which sentence describes the wild cat, not the car? | «Jaguar is a brand I know well» | *«The jaguar hunts caimans in the rainforest» | «The Jaguar is a fast and expensive car» | «Jaguar starts with a capital J»
